Parallel function calling
In addition to single turn function calling, you can also call multiple functions at once. Parallel function calling lets you execute multiple functions at once and is used when the functions are not dependent on each other. This is useful in scenarios like gathering data from multiple independent sources, such as retrieving customer details from different databases or checking inventory levels across various warehouses or performing multiple actions such as converting your apartment into a disco.
When the model initiates multiple function calls in a single turn, you don't need to return the function_result
objects in the same order that the function_call
objects were received. The Gemini API maps each result back to its corresponding call using the tool_use_id
(which matches the call_id
from the model's output). This lets you execute your functions asynchronously and append the results to your list as they complete.
